I seem to dimly recall that a real longbow (shot by a real longbowman)
could easily piece armor at a reasonable distance, and was much more
accurate than a crossbow (at long ranges).  The crossbow was more
effective at short ranges, particularly, since it didn't take gobs of
training to be able to shoot the thing, which a longbow did (ie, the
generals could skimp on paying to train xx longbowmen for years or
months, and just get your average plow jockey to fire it).

One other peeve I have with nethack, is that you should be able to
take things from your pet (here rover, bring me that nice bag of
holding...), and you should be able to attempt rob adjacent unfriendly
monsters of their weapons or treasure (though of course, they will
attack you for it, unlike your pet).
